@dircategory and @direntry are what makeinfo turns into the
INFO-DIR-SECTION block that install-info reads.  Without them a rebuilt
info file drops out of the dir node again, undoing by hand what the
patches against info/ put there.

--- man/gnus.texi.orig	1994-09-11 20:52:45.000000000 +0200
+++ man/gnus.texi
@@ -3,6 +3,12 @@
 @comment %**start of header (This is for running Texinfo on a region.)
 @setfilename ../info/gnus
 @settitle GNUS 3.15 Manual
+
+@dircategory Editors
+@direntry
+* GNUS: (gnus).		The newsreader GNUS.
+@end direntry
+
 @iftex
 @finalout
 @end iftex
